{
  // The pilot Worker (code design §9, H1): Telegram's webhook, the privacy notices, the health
  // check, the API under /v1 (ADR-29), the three queues, cron, and three Durable Objects:
  // MemberScheduler, ReconcileHeartbeat, which /healthz reads for the watchdog
  // (.github/workflows/watchdog.yml), and AccountWriteLimiter, which counts each account's API
  // writes. The admin pages are a second Worker from this package,
  // configured in wrangler.admin.jsonc, because Cloudflare Access protects every hostname of a
  // Worker and would close this one to Telegram, and to the app on a phone.
  //
  // Three environments: the top level is local development (`wrangler dev`), `staging` and
  // `production` are what deploy.yml deploys. Named environments inherit nothing that binds a
  // resource, so every environment repeats its bindings with its own resource names.
  //
  // Hosts (H3). Each deployed Worker answers only on its workers.dev address,
  // https://<Worker name>.<account subdomain>.workers.dev, where the subdomain is the one each
  // Cloudflare account chose at sign-up: `vela-light` for production ("Vela"), `vela-light-staging`
  // for staging ("Vela staging"). There is no domain, zone, or route.
  //
  // This is the one list of what changes if an account's subdomain is not the one above. First,
  // what src/wrangler-config.test.ts holds together, and fails on until every place agrees:
  //   - WORKERS_DEV_SUBDOMAINS in that test, from which it derives every host it expects;
  //   - the three URL vars of that environment here;
  //   - PUBLIC_BASE_URL of that environment in wrangler.admin.jsonc;
  //   - every workers.dev link written into the Markdown of plan/materials/pilot: the two privacy
  //     notices' links to each other, the notice links in the nearby-contact consent texts (en and
  //     zh-TW), which families are sent, in the organiser agreements (en and zh-TW), and in the
  //     pilot README;
  //   - src/notices.generated.ts, which src/notices.test.ts holds to the notices: after changing
  //     their links, run `pnpm --filter @vela/worker notices`.
  // Then what no test can see:
  //   - the privacy policy link of that environment's bot in @BotFather (infra/README.md section 7);
  //   - the Telegram webhook, which the setup script's `webhook` step registers on the origin of
  //     that environment's notice URLs here: run it again with
  //     `pnpm --filter @vela/worker run setup -- --env <environment> --from webhook`;
  //   - the watchdog's URL for that environment in .github/watchdog.json;
  //   - the documents that write the hosts out, which `git grep vela-light` lists.
  //
  // Every `id` or username the founder has not created yet is written as a PLACEHOLDER: replace
  // each with the value Cloudflare or BotFather returns, never a guess. Outside development the
  // Worker refuses to start while any var or secret still holds PLACEHOLDER_, a URL var is not
  // https, or a privacy notice still holds a bracketed blank (src/config.ts).
  //
  // ADMIN_CONVERSATION_ID, the founder's own Telegram chat id, is a secret of this Worker (H5),
  // never a var: `.dev.vars.example` lists it with the other secrets.
  //
  // AI_PROVIDER (decision X, 2026-09-18) is "anthropic" or "off", the same in wrangler.admin.jsonc
  // for each environment. With "off" no AI provider is called: answers get no summary, flag check,
  // or translation, questions no chips, weekly read drafts no lines, and a sent weekly read no
  // translation for her; speech-to-text stays on. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is needed only with
  // "anthropic". Development defaults to "off", so local work needs no key; staging is "off" for
  // the dogfooding week; production must be "anthropic", and src/config.ts refuses to start it
  // otherwise, because families' answers need the flag check. To switch staging on: set
  // "anthropic" for staging here and in wrangler.admin.jsonc and commit, then run
  // `pnpm --filter @vela/worker run setup -- --env staging --from secrets` on that commit before
  // it is merged to main, which asks for the key and deploys. Merged first, CI would deploy
  // staging without the key, and both Workers would refuse to run (ConfigError:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY).
  //
  // MEDIA_STORAGE (decision M, 2026-09-20) is "r2" or "off", and belongs to this Worker alone: the
  // admin Worker stores no media and has no such var. With "off" nothing she sends is copied into
  // Vela's own storage: the light, the family group, and the transcript of a voice answer are
  // unchanged, because Telegram carries the file and the pipeline fetches it from there, but each
  // media row keeps only what Telegram said about the file, its id, its type and its size, with no
  // storage key and no copy of the file itself. An environment that is "off" binds no R2 bucket at
  // all, because a binding to a bucket that does not exist fails the deploy, and src/deps.ts then
  // builds no media port. Development is "off", so a laptop needs no bucket and keeps no copy.
  // Staging is "r2" since 26 September 2026: the founder enabled R2 on the "Vela staging" account
  // (R2 needs a payment method even though the pilot's use stays inside its free monthly
  // allowance), and the co-founder created its bucket, vela-media-staging, so photo asks and
  // voice-note copies run there as in production. Production must be "r2", and src/config.ts
  // refuses to start it otherwise, because the privacy notice promises families that media is kept
  // in Vela's own storage for 30 days and then deleted. To switch an environment on: enable R2 in
  // the Cloudflare dashboard for that account, set "r2" for that environment here and add its
  // r2_buckets binding, commit, then run
  // `pnpm --filter @vela/worker run setup -- --env <environment> --from resources` on that commit
  // before it is merged to main, which creates the bucket and deploys.
  //
  // API_V1 (ADR-29) is "on" or "off": whether this Worker serves the API under /v1, which
  // src/pilot-worker.ts hands to src/api-runtime.ts before any other route, and which checks its
  // own settings (src/config.ts, readApiConfig), so a refusal there answers 503 on /v1 alone.
  // Development and staging are "on"; production is "off", where /v1 answers 404 and nothing below
  // is read, and src/wrangler-config.test.ts pins it off until a new ADR turns it on. CLERK_ISSUER
  // is the Clerk Frontend API origin session tokens are verified against: the development instance
  // in development and staging, and absent in production while its API is off. CLERK_SECRET_KEY,
  // for the live session check on every write, is a secret only the founder puts, never a var: in
  // apps/worker, `pnpm exec wrangler secret put CLERK_SECRET_KEY --env staging`. Staging refuses an
  // issuer that is not *.clerk.accounts.dev or a key that is not a development key (sk_test_), and
  // answers 503 on /v1 without the key; production, once on, refuses a development issuer or key.
  // Two limits admit the API's requests: API_IP_LIMIT, a Workers Rate Limiting binding, which
  // creates no resource, 120 a minute per client address (per /64 for IPv6), a best effort that was
  // never shown to act on workers.dev; and ACCOUNT_WRITE_LIMITER, the AccountWriteLimiter Durable
  // Object, one per account, 20 writes a minute, before the call to Clerk. Production binds neither
  // while its API is off, and readApiConfig refuses to serve the API without them. /v1 has no CORS:
  // OPTIONS answers 404, no Access-Control- header is sent, and a request carrying Origin is refused.
  "$schema": "./node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "vela-dev",
  "main": "src/index.ts",
  // The newest date the Workers Vitest pool's runtime accepts; raise it together with
  // @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers, or `pnpm test` cannot start its runtime.
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-22",
  // node-postgres reaches Postgres through Hyperdrive with the Node compatibility layer.
  "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat"],
  "observability": { "enabled": true },
  // Development is never deployed, so it has no address: `workers_dev` defaults to true and is
  // inherited, and a `wrangler deploy` without --env deploys this top level, which is ENVIRONMENT
  // development, where config.ts skips its refusals. `staging` and `production` turn workers.dev on
  // as their only address. Preview URLs stay off everywhere: a Worker with a Durable Object gets
  // none anyway, and every hostname the Worker answers on is one more to reason about.
  "workers_dev": false,
  "preview_urls": false,

  // The admin Worker binds MemberScheduler by `script_name`; only this Worker, which exports the
  // classes, declares their migrations, which every environment inherits. ReconcileHeartbeat (v2)
  // holds one time, the last finished reconciliation, in a Durable Object rather than in Postgres,
  // so /healthz never wakes Neon. AccountWriteLimiter (v3) counts each account's API writes in an
  // object of its own (src/write-limit.ts); production declares the class but binds none while its
  // API is off.
  "migrations": [
    { "tag": "v1", "new_sqlite_classes": ["MemberScheduler"] },
    { "tag": "v2", "new_sqlite_classes": ["ReconcileHeartbeat"] },
    { "tag": "v3", "new_sqlite_classes": ["AccountWriteLimiter"] }
  ],
  "durable_objects": {
    "bindings": [
      { "name": "MEMBER_SCHEDULER", "class_name": "MemberScheduler" },
      { "name": "RECONCILE_HEARTBEAT", "class_name": "ReconcileHeartbeat" },
      { "name": "ACCOUNT_WRITE_LIMITER", "class_name": "AccountWriteLimiter" }
    ]
  },

  "queues": {
    "producers": [
      { "binding": "OUTBOUND_QUEUE", "queue": "vela-outbound" },
      { "binding": "MEDIA_QUEUE", "queue": "vela-media" },
      { "binding": "UNDERSTAND_QUEUE", "queue": "vela-understand" }
    ],
    // A message is retried until the send or the AI call stops failing, then parked in the
    // dead-letter queue, where the founder can see it rather than lose it.
    "consumers": [
      {
        "queue": "vela-outbound",
        "max_batch_size": 10,
        "max_batch_timeout": 5,
        "max_retries": 5,
        "retry_delay": 30,
        "dead_letter_queue": "vela-dead-letter"
      },
      {
        "queue": "vela-media",
        "max_batch_size": 5,
        "max_batch_timeout": 10,
        "max_retries": 3,
        "retry_delay": 60,
        "dead_letter_queue": "vela-dead-letter"
      },
      {
        "queue": "vela-understand",
        "max_batch_size": 5,
        "max_batch_timeout": 10,
        "max_retries": 3,
        "retry_delay": 60,
        "dead_letter_queue": "vela-dead-letter"
      }
    ]
  },

  // No r2_buckets binding: MEDIA_STORAGE is "off" here, so `wrangler dev` needs no bucket and
  // nothing a laptop run keeps a copy of.

  // `localConnectionString` is `pnpm --filter @vela/db dev-db` (packages/db/scripts/dev-db.ts).
  "hyperdrive": [
    {
      "binding": "HYPERDRIVE",
      "id": "PLACEHOLDER_HYPERDRIVE_ID_DEV",
      "localConnectionString": "postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54320/postgres"
    }
  ],

  // Every 15 minutes: reconcile (pending send effects, stranded sends, late ticks, the understanding
  // re-run and the founder's note, then the heartbeat; flows §3.15). Not every 5: each run wakes
  // Neon, and a 5-minute run would spend the free plan's compute hours (src/pilot-worker.ts).
  // Nightly at 03:20 UTC: yesterday's metrics and retention.
  "triggers": { "crons": ["*/15 * * * *", "20 3 * * *"] },

  // The API's address limit (ADR-29, API_ADDRESS_LIMIT in src/api-runtime.ts): per client address
  // (per /64 for IPv6) before the app, a best effort. The per-account write limit is the
  // ACCOUNT_WRITE_LIMITER binding above.
  "ratelimits": [
    { "name": "API_IP_LIMIT", "namespace_id": "1001", "simple": { "limit": 120, "period": 60 } }
  ],

  "vars": {
    "ENVIRONMENT": "development",
    "TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME": "PLACEHOLDER_DEV_BOT_USERNAME",
    // `pnpm dev` serves this Worker on port 8787; `pnpm dev:admin` serves the admin Worker there
    // instead. On a laptop a link only has to be there.
    "PUBLIC_BASE_URL": "http://localhost:8787",
    "PRIVACY_NOTICE_URL_EN": "http://localhost:8787/privacy",
    "PRIVACY_NOTICE_URL_ZH_TW": "http://localhost:8787/privacy/zh-TW",
    "REGIONS": "apac",
    "AI_PROVIDER": "off",
    "MEDIA_STORAGE": "off",
    "API_V1": "on",
    // Clerk's development instance for Vela Light: public, since the publishable key encodes it.
    "CLERK_ISSUER": "https://ideal-vulture-9262.clerk.accounts.dev"
  },

  "env": {
    "staging": {
      "name": "vela",
      "workers_dev": true,
      "preview_urls": false,
      "observability": { "enabled": true },
      "durable_objects": {
        "bindings": [
          { "name": "MEMBER_SCHEDULER", "class_name": "MemberScheduler" },
          { "name": "RECONCILE_HEARTBEAT", "class_name": "ReconcileHeartbeat" },
          { "name": "ACCOUNT_WRITE_LIMITER", "class_name": "AccountWriteLimiter" }
        ]
      },
      "queues": {
        "producers": [
          { "binding": "OUTBOUND_QUEUE", "queue": "vela-outbound-staging" },
          { "binding": "MEDIA_QUEUE", "queue": "vela-media-staging" },
          { "binding": "UNDERSTAND_QUEUE", "queue": "vela-understand-staging" }
        ],
        "consumers": [
          {
            "queue": "vela-outbound-staging",
            "max_batch_size": 10,
            "max_batch_timeout": 5,
            "max_retries": 5,
            "retry_delay": 30,
            "dead_letter_queue": "vela-dead-letter-staging"
          },
          {
            "queue": "vela-media-staging",
            "max_batch_size": 5,
            "max_batch_timeout": 10,
            "max_retries": 3,
            "retry_delay": 60,
            "dead_letter_queue": "vela-dead-letter-staging"
          },
          {
            "queue": "vela-understand-staging",
            "max_batch_size": 5,
            "max_batch_timeout": 10,
            "max_retries": 3,
            "retry_delay": 60,
            "dead_letter_queue": "vela-dead-letter-staging"
          }
        ]
      },
      // MEDIA_STORAGE is "r2" here since 26 September 2026: the founder enabled R2 on the staging
      // account, and the co-founder created this bucket (private, Asia-Pacific).
      "r2_buckets": [{ "binding": "MEDIA_BUCKET", "bucket_name": "vela-media-staging" }],
      "hyperdrive": [{ "binding": "HYPERDRIVE", "id": "e9e9837d1eee47528304916a1ac2d1e9" }],
      "triggers": { "crons": ["*/15 * * * *", "20 3 * * *"] },
      "ratelimits": [
        {
          "name": "API_IP_LIMIT",
          "namespace_id": "1001",
          "simple": { "limit": 120, "period": 60 }
        }
      ],
      "vars": {
        "ENVIRONMENT": "staging",
        "TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME": "VelaLightstagingbot",
        // The admin Worker's origin: links in the founder's admin messages open it.
        "PUBLIC_BASE_URL": "https://vela-admin.vela-light-staging.workers.dev",
        // This Worker's origin and the notice paths it serves (src/notices.ts).
        "PRIVACY_NOTICE_URL_EN": "https://vela.vela-light-staging.workers.dev/privacy",
        "PRIVACY_NOTICE_URL_ZH_TW": "https://vela.vela-light-staging.workers.dev/privacy/zh-TW",
        "REGIONS": "apac",
        // Off for the dogfooding week, until the founder approves buying Anthropic credit.
        "AI_PROVIDER": "off",
        // On since 26 September 2026, bound to vela-media-staging above: voice notes and photos
        // are copied there and deleted after 30 days, as in production.
        "MEDIA_STORAGE": "r2",
        // Staging's app accounts are all test accounts (the dogfooding week's friend has none),
        // so it verifies tokens from Clerk's development instance, as development does.
        "API_V1": "on",
        "CLERK_ISSUER": "https://ideal-vulture-9262.clerk.accounts.dev"
      }
    },

    "production": {
      "name": "vela",
      "workers_dev": true,
      "preview_urls": false,
      "observability": { "enabled": true },
      "durable_objects": {
        "bindings": [
          { "name": "MEMBER_SCHEDULER", "class_name": "MemberScheduler" },
          { "name": "RECONCILE_HEARTBEAT", "class_name": "ReconcileHeartbeat" }
        ]
      },
      "queues": {
        "producers": [
          { "binding": "OUTBOUND_QUEUE", "queue": "vela-outbound-production" },
          { "binding": "MEDIA_QUEUE", "queue": "vela-media-production" },
          { "binding": "UNDERSTAND_QUEUE", "queue": "vela-understand-production" }
        ],
        "consumers": [
          {
            "queue": "vela-outbound-production",
            "max_batch_size": 10,
            "max_batch_timeout": 5,
            "max_retries": 5,
            "retry_delay": 30,
            "dead_letter_queue": "vela-dead-letter-production"
          },
          {
            "queue": "vela-media-production",
            "max_batch_size": 5,
            "max_batch_timeout": 10,
            "max_retries": 3,
            "retry_delay": 60,
            "dead_letter_queue": "vela-dead-letter-production"
          },
          {
            "queue": "vela-understand-production",
            "max_batch_size": 5,
            "max_batch_timeout": 10,
            "max_retries": 3,
            "retry_delay": 60,
            "dead_letter_queue": "vela-dead-letter-production"
          }
        ]
      },
      "r2_buckets": [{ "binding": "MEDIA_BUCKET", "bucket_name": "vela-media-production" }],
      "hyperdrive": [{ "binding": "HYPERDRIVE", "id": "PLACEHOLDER_HYPERDRIVE_ID_PRODUCTION" }],
      "triggers": { "crons": ["*/15 * * * *", "20 3 * * *"] },
      "vars": {
        "ENVIRONMENT": "production",
        "TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME": "PLACEHOLDER_PRODUCTION_BOT_USERNAME",
        "PUBLIC_BASE_URL": "https://vela-admin.vela-light.workers.dev",
        "PRIVACY_NOTICE_URL_EN": "https://vela.vela-light.workers.dev/privacy",
        "PRIVACY_NOTICE_URL_ZH_TW": "https://vela.vela-light.workers.dev/privacy/zh-TW",
        "REGIONS": "apac",
        "AI_PROVIDER": "anthropic",
        "MEDIA_STORAGE": "r2",
        // Off until a new ADR turns it on (ADR-29): no CLERK_ISSUER, no ratelimits, and no
        // ACCOUNT_WRITE_LIMITER binding until then.
        "API_V1": "off"
      }
    }
  }
}
